&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About AppLovin&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.applovin.com&amp;amp;esheet=54549558&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260608414458&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AppLovin&amp;amp;index=3&amp;amp;md5=a4ac8b1dcb8b5502d0154df68e322df6&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AppLovin&lt;/a&gt; makes technologies that help businesses of every size connect to their ideal customers. The company provides end-to-end advertising solutions for businesses to reach, monetize and grow their global audiences. For more information about AppLovin, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.applovin.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.applovin.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;To deliver on this mission, our global team is composed of team members with life experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives that mirror our developers and customers around the world. At AppLovin, we are intentional about the team and culture we are building, seeking candidates who are outstanding in their own right and also demonstrate their support of others.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;AppLovin is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Measurement Data Scientist&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to join our Product Partnerships &amp;amp; Measurement team. This role is ideal for someone who is deeply curious about data and metrics—someone who doesn’t just analyze numbers, but strives to understand the nuances, assumptions, and limitations behind them. You’ll play a key role in helping us triangulate across multiple sources of truth—platform data, 3rd-party measurement (MMM, MTA, incrementality, post purchase survey, etc), and internal attribution systems—to uncover actionable insights that drive smarter business and marketing decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll collaborate closely with the Partnerships, Marketing Science, and Business Development teams to interpret results, refine methodologies, and translate insights into strategies that drive impact for AppLovin, our partners, and advertisers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate performance metrics across platform and 3rd-party measurement systems to identify inconsistencies, uncover insights, and drive clarity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze data using SQL and Python (pandas, numpy, sklearn, matplotlib) to extract trends and inform business decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize complex data into clear, actionable insights and communicate them effectively across technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a strong understanding of advertising and commerce ecosystems, including conversion tracking, attribution, media mix modeling and incrementality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal and external stakeholders to design and evaluate incrementality tests, and to interpret results and insights from MMM, MTA, brand lift, post-purchase studies, and other measurement frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ask critical questions, challenge assumptions, and continuously refine the metrics and frameworks used for evaluating performance and provide guidance to advertisers on their learning agendas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tracking frameworks to monitor test performance and campaign outcomes; follow up and follow through with advertisers and partners to ensure best-practice setup, proper tracking, and adoption of key learnings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally to translate analytical findings into business strategies that improve campaign effectiveness and advertiser ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in advertising, digital marketing, or eCommerce analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL skills and experience with large-scale data manipulation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough understanding of data structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Python for data analysis (pandas, numpy, sklearn, matplotlib)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in data analysis in an online environment, with direct exposure to scoping and executing analytical projects end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and ability to translate analytical findings into clear business recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly curious and detail-oriented, with an investigative mindset and comfort working with messy or incomplete data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage competing priorities and deliver results in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and flexible team player who takes initiative and drives continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in advertising, digital marketing, or eCommerce analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with industry-standard measurement methodologies, including CLS, RCTs, attribution modeling, incrementality testing, and GeoLift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to apply AI techniques to marketing measurement challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;AppLovin provides a competitive total compensation package with a pay for performance rewards approach. Total compensation at AppLovin is based on a number of factors including market location and may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. Depending on the position offered, equity, and other forms of incentive compensation (as applicable) may be provided as part of a total compensation package, in addition to dental, vision, and other benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
